From 909e1df865d2fbb4329d1149829219bcfb6962e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:02:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pf: accept unfinished offloaded checksums when sending a
 reset

A TCP packet sent by this host, or by a VNET jail on it over an epair,
with the checksum left to offload carries CSUM_IP_TCP (CSUM_IP6_TCP) and
only the pseudo-header sum in th_sum. pf_check_proto_cksum() computed the
checksum in software, found it wrong and counted proto-cksum, so a
"block return" rule matching it sent no RST: a jail connecting to a
rejected address waited for the connect timeout instead of failing at
once. tcp_input() and udp_input() accept such packets ("Packet from
local host (maybe from a VM)"); do the same.

Seen with Kubernetes pods (VNET jails) connecting to a Service without
endpoints, which kube-proxy rejects with block return.
---
 sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c b/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
index 7aee28e7b..412258912 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
+++ b/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
@@ -9735,6 +9735,14 @@ pf_check_proto_cksum(struct mbuf *m, int off, int len, u_int8_t p, sa_family_t a
 			}
 			sum ^= 0xffff;
 			++hw_assist;
+		} else if (m->m_pkthdr.csum_flags & (CSUM_IP_TCP | CSUM_IP6_TCP)) {
+			/*
+			 * Sent by this host or a VNET jail on it with the
+			 * checksum left to offload, as tcp_input() and
+			 * udp_input() accept: the checksum field isn't
+			 * filled in yet.
+			 */
+			++hw_assist;
 		}
 		break;
 	case IPPROTO_UDP:
@@ -9749,6 +9757,14 @@ pf_check_proto_cksum(struct mbuf *m, int off, int len, u_int8_t p, sa_family_t a
 			}
 			sum ^= 0xffff;
 			++hw_assist;
+		} else if (m->m_pkthdr.csum_flags & (CSUM_IP_UDP | CSUM_IP6_UDP)) {
+			/*
+			 * Sent by this host or a VNET jail on it with the
+			 * checksum left to offload, as tcp_input() and
+			 * udp_input() accept: the checksum field isn't
+			 * filled in yet.
+			 */
+			++hw_assist;
 		}
 		break;
 	case IPPROTO_ICMP:
